# The completion check (decision 0081): a commit whose subject opens
# `feat(cut:<id>): ` is compared with the ledger, and when the ledger shows cut
# <id> neither complete nor integrated, a warning naming the cut, its phase and
# every work package not approved is written to this commit's output, asking its
# author to report the gap as a defect in how the ledger captures the harness's
# events. It is silent otherwise, never refuses (the commit is already made) and
# never writes the ledger. It is `cratylus completion-check`, run from source
# (`tsx`), so it needs no build.
pnpm --silent --filter @cratylus/runtime completion-check || true
